@laoyuehanni/dsh-git-worktree README · Features：- **Commit graph**: expand the branch popup in place to browse branches on the left and their real commit history and merge graph on the right. Browsing does not check out a branch. Select a commit to see its author, date, full message and file summary; bodies start with a three-line preview and expand into an internally scrolling area. History loads the next page when its list scrolls to the end, and a Load more button remains; search covers loaded titles and hashes. The author menu lists every author on the branch and keeps that list in memory for the commit; a branch update, fetch, or reload drops the cache.
- **IDEA-style branch picker**: the branch menu treats `/` as a folder hierarchy — collapsible folders, last-segment labels, the checked-out branch's chain opens centered. Local and remote branches render as two collapsible groups (a single remote strips its prefix), with bottom search (ancestor folders kept, hits highlighted), locate-current-branch and expand/collapse tools, and green ↗N / blue ↙N divergence marks on tracking branches.
- **Remote branch checkout**: pick `origin/feat-x` in the remote group and it checks out in

